              "jcr:created": "Wed Nov 30 2022 19:52:03 GMT+0000",
              "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
              "text": "<h1><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"fontsize-2em\">Reshaping fecal management</span></span></span></h1>\n<h2>hygh-tec is now part of Stryker</h2>\n<p><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Up to 40% of ICU patients experience fecal incontinence,<sup>1</sup> a challenge that can increase the risk of skin injury, infection and distress for patients. That’s why we’re introducing a solution to support your commitment to high-quality patient care.</span></span></p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Feb 23 2026 18:07:48 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            },
            "curatedcta": {
